@* A text input that commits its value as the user types. InputText, and every component deriving from InputBase, commits
   on the browser's change event, which a field raises only when it loses focus; an edit typed with the focus still in the
   field has therefore not reached .NET when the document unloads, and the unsaved-changes guard, which knows nothing but
   its HasUnsavedChanges parameter, has nothing to guard. This is the same input bound on the input event instead, so a
   reload, a typed address or Back asks before it discards the edit. Everything else is InputText: the same Value
   binding, the same EditContext notification on each commit, the same validation class and the same name attribute.
   Writing @bind-Value:event="oninput" on InputText itself compiles but throws while rendering (Arg_ObjObjEx,
   ChangeEventArgs to String), because the handler it puts on the element is typed for the component's own callback. *@
@inherits InputText

<input @attributes="AdditionalAttributes" name="@OmitWhenEmpty(NameAttributeValue)" class="@OmitWhenEmpty(CssClass)"
       @bind="CurrentValueAsString" @bind:event="oninput" @ref="Element"/>

@code {

    // InputText leaves each of the two attributes out when its value is empty, while a razor attribute is left out only
    // for null
    private static string? OmitWhenEmpty(string? value)
    {
        return string.IsNullOrEmpty(value) ? null : value;
    }

}
